							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Kin&#039;s right, the time requirements for ldon were crazy.&nbsp; And I hunted it quite a bit and got a number of upgrades, but it sure wasn&#039;t the fast route to success.&nbsp; As he knows, 6 hours for that 1100 hp aug is an extraordinarily optimistic estimate.&nbsp; For most you&#039;d need to multiply that number by 2 to 4 times, plus excessive LFG time could make it even longer.&nbsp; The lack of variety in the zones really got old fast.&nbsp; <br /><br />Even now most everything about EQ remains a huge timesink.&nbsp; Of course raiding continues to require large blocks of time.&nbsp; The sink has also been brought home again as I try to get the faction for tier 1 oow armor, some fairly nice armor that is designed so that non raiders can get it.&nbsp; Somewhere around 2,000+ faction hits are needed to get high enough faction.&nbsp; Of course not all mobs in OoW have the faction hits.&nbsp; Killing harder mobs in places like PG does not appear to yield anymore faction per hit than killing a greenie in Dranik&#039;s Scar.&nbsp; But of course slaughtering those greenies really gets mind numbing.&nbsp; This crap just takes a really long time.&nbsp; They don&#039;t seem to want more casual players to do this stuff and if they try, they better do almost nothing but faction mobs whenever they&#039;re online.&nbsp; <br />/grinding through amiable right now.... bleh... 
